normalization*)\nmaxDerivative = MaxValue[{Abs[fPrimeNum[x]], -10 <= x <= \
10}, x];\n\n(*Define a color function based on the magnitude and sign of the \
\\\nderivative*)\ncolorFunction[x_] := \n ColorData[\"TemperatureMap\"][0.5 + \
0.5 fPrimeNum[x]/maxDerivative]\n\nPlot[f[x], {x, -10, 10}, PlotStyle -> \
